    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key to be the single source of duplicate detection, per the spec.\n\n**Identity key (`OwnerIdentity.java`)** \u2014 now the lower-case SHA-256 hex digest of `normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + lowerEmail + \"|\" + soundex(lastName)` (previously a plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` composite). This satisfies the `[0-9a-f]{64}` shape the test asserts. Added an `of(telephone, email, lastName)` overload so the key can be built identically from a request body or a stored owner.\n\n**Soundex (`Soundex.java`, new)** \u2014 standard American Soundex (letter + three digits), used for both the key's name segment and the soft-match surname comparison.\n\n**Duplicate 409 (`ValidateUniqueIdentity.java`)** \u2014 replaced the household-id block with a single identity-key scan: reject with 409 when an existing **active** owner (soft-deleted ignored via `ActiveOwners`) carries the identical key. The email-domain blocklist still runs first, in `ValidateNewOwner`.\n\n**Soft match (`PossibleDuplicate.java`)** \u2014 now triggers when the identity keys *differ* but `soundex(lastName)` and postcode *match*. Removed the old \"declared household member\" suppression and the different-telephone condition, so two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones are now created (different keys) and flagged as soft matches of each other rather than rejected.\n\n**Cleanup** \u2014 removed the now-unused `Household.hasMember` and updated the stale Javadoc/YAML comments and the OpenAPI `identityKey`/`possibleDuplicate(Of)` descriptions. The household id is retained purely for the household-size and membership-level rules, which were out of scope.\n\nThe behavioural changes requested \u2014 soft match on soundex+postcode, same-surname/postcode/different-phone no longer a hard duplicate, and the removal of the household-derived 409 block \u2014 are all in place.",
